    "problem_statement": "# print_dashboard writes to stderr instead of stdout\n\nGrafanalib version: latest\n\nWhen using the `print_dashboard` function, the dashboard JSON is being written to stderr instead of stdout. This breaks compatibility with tools that expect the output on stdout, and causes issues when piping the output to other commands.\n\n## Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate a simple dashboard script:\n\n```python\nfrom grafanalib.core import Dashboard\nfrom grafanalib._gen import print_dashboard\n\ndashboard = Dashboard(\n    title=\"Test Dashboard\",\n    rows=[],\n)\n\nprint_dashboard(dashboard)\n```\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nThe dashboard JSON should be printed to stdout, allowing it to be piped to other commands like:\n\n```\npython dashboard.py | jq\n```\n\n## Actual behavior\n\nThe dashboard JSON is printed to stderr, making it impossible to pipe the output to other commands. When trying to pipe the output, nothing appears in the piped command.\n\nThis also breaks compatibility with existing scripts and workflows that expect the output on stdout.\n\n<END WRITING>"
